5.0 cm apart against p.d.: V = 1000, 2000, 3000, 4000 V give F = 0.85, 1.70, 2.55, 3.40 mN, a straight line through the origin.'),
('ed6ff597-304f-5dfe-aa8d-615a0498bec7', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'ea6e0ded-f55f-54ce-803b-1143224c470a', 'a-level', '21.3', '9702 coursebook 21.3 · Uniform electric fields', 46, 46, 'Protons are released from rest at the positive plate of a pair of parallel plates 8.0 mm apart, with a p.d. of 2.0 kV between them. (a) Calculate the acceleration of a proton. (b) Calculate the time it takes to cross the gap, in ns. (c) Calculate its speed at the negative plate, and check it using energy. Give only the answer to (b). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₚ = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '25.85 ns', 'ns', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a = eV/(md) = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2000 ÷ (1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ × 8.0 × 10⁻³) = 2.40 × 10¹³ m s⁻². (b) t = √(2d/a) = √(2 × 8.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2.395 × 10¹³) = 2.58 × 10⁻⁸ s. In ns: 2.585 × 10⁻⁸ × 10⁹ = 25.8. (c) v = at = 2.395 × 10¹³ × 2.585 × 10⁻⁸ = 6.19 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹; energy gives √(2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2000 ÷ 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷) = 6.19 × 10⁵ m s⁻¹, the same. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: E = V/d and a = eE/m. C1: t = √(2d/a). C1: conversion to ns. C1: v = at. B1: energy check agrees. A1: t = 25.8 ns.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg5aefa210-t fg5aefa210-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg5aefa210-t">Protons crossing the gap</title><desc id="fg5aefa210-d">Parallel plates 8.0 mm apart with a p.d. of 2.0 kV; protons are released from rest at the positive (top) plate.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="78" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text><line x1="110" y1="56" x2="110" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,164 107,157.7 113,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="56" x2="140" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="140,164 137,157.7 143,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="170" y1="56" x2="170" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,164 167,157.7 173,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="200" y1="56" x2="200" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,164 197,157.7 203,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="230" y1="56" x2="230" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,164 227,157.7 233,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="260" y1="56" x2="260" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="260,164 257,157.7 263,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="290" y1="56" x2="290" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="290,164 287,157.7 293,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><polygon points="332,50 335,56.3 329,56.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="332" y1="54.9" x2="332" y2="165.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="332,170 329,163.7 335,163.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="338" y="110" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 mm</text><text x="200" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 kV</text><circle cx="200" cy="59.6" r="8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="200" y="60.1" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);font-weight:700">+</text><text x="212" y="47.6" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309)">proton</text></svg>', 'Parallel plates 8.0 mm apart with a p.d. of 2.0 kV; protons are released from rest at the positive (top) plate.'),
('9cce3823-8476-517e-87f7-a1a1eb9399c0', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'ea6e0ded-f55f-54ce-803b-1143224c470a', 'a-level', '21.3', '9702 coursebook 21.3 · Uniform electric fields', 47, 47, 'In an electrostatic air cleaner, air flows at 2.0 m s⁻¹ between two parallel plates that are 30 cm long and 2.0 cm apart, with 8.0 kV between them. A dust particle of mass 1.0 × 10⁻¹⁵ kg carries a charge of 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁷ C and enters halfway between the plates. (a) Calculate the field strength. (b) Ignoring air resistance and gravity, calculate the acceleration of the particle across the gap. (c) Calculate how far the particle travels along the plates before it reaches one of them, in mm. Give only the answer to (c).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.536 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 8.0 × 10³ ÷ 0.020 = 4.0 × 10⁵ V m⁻¹. (b) a = QE/m = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁷ × 4.0 × 10⁵ ÷ 1.0 × 10⁻¹⁵ = 6400 m s⁻². (c) It must move 1.0 cm sideways: t = √(2 × 0.010 ÷ 6400) = 0.00177 s. Distance along = 2.0 × 0.001768 = 0.00354 m. In mm: 0.003536 × 1000 = 3.54. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: E = V/d. C1: a = QE/m. M1: sideways distance 1.0 cm from rest. C1: t from s = ½at². C1: distance = air speed × t. A1: x = 3.54 mm.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg93d93176-t fg93d93176-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg93d93176-t">Electrostatic air cleaner</title><desc id="fg93d93176-d">Air flows at 2.0 m s⁻¹ between parallel plates 30 cm long and 2.0 cm apart with 8.0 kV between them; a charged dust particle enters halfway between the plates.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="78" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text><line x1="110" y1="56" x2="110" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,164 107,157.7 113,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="56" x2="140" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="140,164 137,157.7 143,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="170" y1="56" x2="170" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,164 167,157.7 173,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="200" y1="56" x2="200" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,164 197,157.7 203,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="230" y1="56" x2="230" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,164 227,157.7 233,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="260" y1="56" x2="260" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="260,164 257,157.7 263,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="290" y1="56" x2="290" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="290,164 287,157.7 293,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><polygon points="332,50 335,56.3 329,56.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="332" y1="54.9" x2="332" y2="165.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="332,170 329,163.7 335,163.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="338" y="110" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0 cm</text><polygon points="90,196 96.3,193 96.3,199" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="94.9" y1="196" x2="305.1" y2="196" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="310,196 303.7,199 303.7,193" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="200" y="208" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">30 cm</text><text x="200" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">8.0 kV</text><line x1="20" y1="110" x2="79.7" y2="110" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="86,110 77.8,113.8 77.8,106.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><text x="22" y="96" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">air at 2.0 m s⁻¹</text><line x1="90" y1="110" x2="350" y2="110" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:6 4"/></svg>', 'Air flows at 2.0 m s⁻¹ between parallel plates 30 cm long and 2.0 cm apart with 8.0 kV between them; a charged dust particle enters halfway between the plates.'),
('34b67e82-b34b-58df-95e7-10c576ac14e7', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'ea6e0ded-f55f-54ce-803b-1143224c470a', 'a-level', '21.3', '9702 coursebook 21.3 · Uniform electric fields', 48, 48, 'Two parallel plates 12 cm apart are at 0 V and +600 V. (a) Calculate the field strength. (b) Calculate the potential at a point 4.0 cm from the 0 V plate. (c) An electron moves from the point 4.0 cm from the 0 V plate to a point 10.0 cm from it. Calculate the work done on the electron by the field, in units of 10⁻¹⁷ J. Give only the answer to (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.8', '10⁻¹⁷ J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 600 ÷ 0.12 = 5000 V m⁻¹. (b) V = 5000 × 0.040 = 200 V. (c) At 10.0 cm, V = 5000 × 0.100 = 500 V. The electron moves towards higher potential, so the field does positive work: W = eΔV = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × (500 − 200) = 4.80 × 10⁻¹⁷ J. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: E = V/d. C1: V = Ex. M1: W = QΔV. B1: positive work for electron moving to higher V. A1: W = 4.80 × 10⁻¹⁷ J.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg7eae891c-t fg7eae891c-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg7eae891c-t">Plates at 0 V and +600 V</title><desc id="fg7eae891c-d">Parallel plates 12 cm apart: the top plate is at +600 V and the bottom plate at 0 V.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+600 V</text><text x="78" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">0 V</text><line x1="110" y1="56" x2="110" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,164 107,157.7 113,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="56" x2="140" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="140,164 137,157.7 143,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="170" y1="56" x2="170" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,164 167,157.7 173,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="200" y1="56" x2="200" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,164 197,157.7 203,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="230" y1="56" x2="230" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,164 227,157.7 233,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="260" y1="56" x2="260" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="260,164 257,157.7 263,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="290" y1="56" x2="290" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="290,164 287,157.7 293,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><polygon points="332,50 335,56.3 329,56.3" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="332" y1="54.9" x2="332" y2="165.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="332,170 329,163.7 335,163.7" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="338" y="110" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">12 cm</text></svg>', 'Parallel plates 12 cm apart: the top plate is at +600 V and the bottom plate at 0 V.'),
('1e8e3e4f-471b-507e-a0ba-49a85acaf6f6', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'ea6e0ded-f55f-54ce-803b-1143224c470a', 'a-level', '21.3', '9702 coursebook 21.3 · Uniform electric fields', 49, 49, '(a) An electron accelerated through a p.d. V_a enters, midway and parallel, between deflecting plates of length L and separation d with p.d. V_p. Show that its deflection on leaving the plates is y = V_p L² ÷ (4V_a d). (b) For L = 3.0 cm, d = 0.80 cm and V_a = 2000 V, calculate the deflecting p.d. needed to give y = 2.0 mm. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '142.2', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) ½mv² = eV_a gives v² = 2eV_a/m. t = L/v and a = eV_p/(md). y = ½at² = ½ × (eV_p/md) × L²m/(2eV_a) = V_p L²/(4V_a d). (b) V_p = 4V_a dy/L² = 4 × 2000 × 0.0080 × 0.0020 ÷ 0.030² = 142 V. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: v² = 2eV_a/m. C1: t = L/v and a = eV_p/(md). M1: substitution into y = ½at². B1: result shown. C1: rearranged for V_p. A1: V_p = 142 V.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('525b1fbf-05c3-5c2b-9f3f-5f0e6d327307', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'ea6e0ded-f55f-54ce-803b-1143224c470a', 'a-level', '21.3', '9702 coursebook 21.3 · Uniform electric fields', 50, 50, 'An ion thruster on a spacecraft accelerates singly charged xenon ions (mass 2.18 × 10⁻²⁵ kg) from rest through 1.2 kV between two grids 1.0 mm apart. (a) Calculate the field strength between the grids. (b) Calculate the exit speed of the ions. (c) The thruster emits 3.0 × 10¹⁸ ions per second. Calculate the thrust, in mN. Give only the answer to (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '27.45 mN', 'mN', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = 1200 ÷ 1.0 × 10⁻³ = 1.2 × 10⁶ V m⁻¹. (b) v = √(2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 1200 ÷ 2.18 × 10⁻²⁵) = 4.20 × 10⁴ m s⁻¹. (c) Thrust = rate of change of momentum = 3.0 × 10¹⁸ × 2.18 × 10⁻²⁵ × 4.197 × 10⁴ = 0.0274 N. In mN: 0.02745 × 1000 = 27.4. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: E = V/d. C1: ½mv² = eV. M1: F = (number per second) × mv. C1: substitution. C1: conversion to mN. A1: F = 27.4 mN.', 6, NULL, NULL)
