22.1 329.8,222.6 330.5,223.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'Path of one type of particle falling from rest between vertical plates with a horizontal field of 5.0 × 10⁵ N C⁻¹ and charge-to-mass ratio 2.0 × 10⁻⁶ C kg⁻¹: a straight line slanting sideways as it falls 1.0 m.'),
('fd315175-e967-5007-9266-6aa59e990514', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'd1772ef2-4c08-4e93-86a4-2802dcbf78cc', 'a-level', '21.4', '9702 coursebook 21.4 · Force on a charge', 46, 46, 'In an experiment, the acceleration of identical ions is measured in different uniform fields: E/10⁴ N C⁻¹ = 1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0 and a/10¹² m s⁻² = 0.96, 1.92, 2.88, 3.84. (a) Show that a is proportional to E. (b) Calculate the gradient of the graph of a against E and state what it represents. (c) Each ion carries charge +e. Calculate the mass of an ion, in units of 10⁻²⁷ kg, and identify the ion. Give only the mass from (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.667', '10⁻²⁷ kg', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) a/E = 0.96 × 10¹² ÷ 1.0 × 10⁴ = 9.6 × 10⁷ for every reading, so a ∝ E. (b) Gradient = (3.84 − 0.96) × 10¹² ÷ ((4.0 − 1.0) × 10⁴) = 9.6 × 10⁷ C kg⁻¹, which is Q/m since a = (Q/m)E. (c) m = e ÷ gradient = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 9.6 × 10⁷ = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg: a proton (hydrogen ion). Mark scheme (6 marks). B1: a/E constant. C1: gradient. M1: gradient = Q/m. C1: m = e/gradient. B1: identifies proton. A1: m = 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 410" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgfe937bdb-t fgfe937bdb-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgfe937bdb-t">Acceleration against field strength</title><desc id="fgfe937bdb-d">Table and graph of ion acceleration against field strength: E = 1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0 × 10⁴ N C⁻¹ give a = 0.96, 1.92, 2.88, 3.84 × 10¹² m s⁻², a straight line through the origin.</desc><g transform="translate(0,0)"><rect x="88.4" y="8" width="223.1" height="140" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="88.4" y="8" width="223.1" height="28" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="142.8" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">E / 10⁴ N C⁻¹</text><text x="254.4" y="22" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">a / 10¹² m s⁻²</text><line x1="197.3" y1="8" x2="197.3" y2="148" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="88.4" y1="36" x2="311.6" y2="36" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="142.8" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.0</text><text x="254.4" y="50" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.96</text><line x1="88.4" y1="64" x2="311.6" y2="64" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="142.8" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.0</text><text x="254.4" y="78" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1.92</text><line x1="88.4" y1="92" x2="311.6" y2="92" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="142.8" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3.0</text><text x="254.4" y="106" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2.88</text><line x1="88.4" y1="120" x2="311.6" y2="120" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="142.8" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4.0</text><text x="254.4" y="134" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3.84</text></g><g transform="translate(0,160)"><line x1="24" y1="34" x2="24" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="105.4" y1="34" x2="105.4" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="186.7" y1="34" x2="186.7" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="268.1" y1="34" x2="268.1" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="349.5" y1="34" x2="349.5" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="382" y2="202" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="162" x2="382" y2="162" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="122" x2="382" y2="122" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="82" x2="382" y2="82" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="42" x2="382" y2="42" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="388" y2="202" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="24" y2="28" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="392,202 385.7,205 385.7,199" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><polygon points="24,24 27,30.3 21,30.3" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><line x1="24" y1="202" x2="24" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="24" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="105.4" y1="202" x2="105.4" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="105.4" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="186.7" y1="202" x2="186.7" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="186.7" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="268.1" y1="202" x2="268.1" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="268.1" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="349.5" y1="202" x2="349.5" y2="206" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="349.5" y="214" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><line x1="20" y1="202" x2="24" y2="202" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="202" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0</text><line x1="20" y1="162" x2="24" y2="162" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="162" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">1</text><line x1="20" y1="122" x2="24" y2="122" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="122" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">2</text><line x1="20" y1="82" x2="24" y2="82" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="82" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">3</text><line x1="20" y1="42" x2="24" y2="42" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="17" y="42" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">4</text><text x="203" y="234" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">E / 10⁴ N C⁻¹</text><text x="20" y="14" font-size="14" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">a / 10¹² m s⁻²</text><line x1="101.4" y1="159.6" x2="109.4" y2="167.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="101.4" y1="167.6" x2="109.4" y2="159.6" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="182.7" y1="121.2" x2="190.7" y2="129.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="182.7" y1="129.2" x2="190.7" y2="121.2" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.1" y1="82.8" x2="272.1" y2="90.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="264.1" y1="90.8" x2="272.1" y2="82.8" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="345.5" y1="44.4" x2="353.5" y2="52.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="345.5" y1="52.4" x2="353.5" y2="44.4" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></g></svg>', 'Table and graph of ion acceleration against field strength: E = 1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0 × 10⁴ N C⁻¹ give a = 0.96, 1.92, 2.88, 3.84 × 10¹² m s⁻², a straight line through the origin.'),
('4ecac8f7-f26a-53f6-ad52-406b8203a779', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'd1772ef2-4c08-4e93-86a4-2802dcbf78cc', 'a-level', '21.4', '9702 coursebook 21.4 · Force on a charge', 47, 47, 'An electron starts from rest and is accelerated through a distance of 4.0 cm by a uniform field of 2.5 × 10⁴ N C⁻¹. (a) Calculate the work done on the electron by the field. (b) Express its kinetic energy in electronvolts. (c) Calculate its final speed. Give only the answer to (c). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.874e7', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) W = eEd = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 2.5 × 10⁴ × 0.040 = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁶ J. (b) The p.d. crossed is Ed = 2.5 × 10⁴ × 0.040 = 1000 V, so E_k = 1000 eV. (c) v = √(2W/m) = √(2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁶ ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹) = 1.87 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: W = Fd = eEd. C1: E_k in eV. M1: W = ½mv². C1: substitution. A1: v = 1.87 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('de2d4fdc-3979-580d-8eac-d3ed232f4555', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'd1772ef2-4c08-4e93-86a4-2802dcbf78cc', 'a-level', '21.4', '9702 coursebook 21.4 · Force on a charge', 48, 48, 'A simple pendulum has a bob of mass 0.050 kg carrying a charge of +5.0 µC on a string 0.80 m long. It swings in a uniform downward electric field of 4.0 × 10⁴ N C⁻¹. (a) Calculate the electric force on the bob. (b) Calculate the effective gravitational field strength acting on the bob. (c) Calculate the period of small oscillations. (d) State how the period would change if the charge were negative. Give only the answer to (c). Take g = 9.81 m s⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.512', 's', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) F = QE = 5.0 × 10⁻⁶ × 4.0 × 10⁴ = 0.20 N, downwards. (b) g_eff = 9.81 + 0.20 ÷ 0.050 = 13.81 N kg⁻¹. (c) T = 2π√(l/g_eff) = 2π × √(0.80 ÷ 13.81) = 1.51 s. (d) The electric force would act upwards, reducing g_eff to 5.81 N kg⁻¹, so the period would increase. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: F = QE. M1: g_eff = g + F/m. C1: T = 2π√(l/g). C1: substitution. B1: period increases for negative charge. A1: T = 1.51 s.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('509baff2-2650-50ea-befc-02f58e140f9f', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'd1772ef2-4c08-4e93-86a4-2802dcbf78cc', 'a-level', '21.4', '9702 coursebook 21.4 · Force on a charge', 49, 49, 'An oil drop carrying three excess electrons is held stationary between horizontal plates when the p.d. is 600 V. (a) Explain why a larger charge needs a smaller p.d. to hold the drop still. (b) The drop gains one more electron. Calculate the p.d. now needed to keep it stationary. (c) State what happens if the p.d. is left at 600 V. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '450', 'V', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) For balance QV/d = mg, so V = mgd/Q: with m and d fixed, V ∝ 1/Q. (b) V = 600 × 3 ÷ 4 = 450 V. (c) The electric force (4e × 600/d) is now larger than the weight, so the drop accelerates upwards. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: QV/d = mg. B1: V ∝ 1/Q. C1: substitution. B1: drop moves upwards. A1: V = 450 V.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 230" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg98ffa748-t fg98ffa748-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg98ffa748-t">Stationary oil drop</title><desc id="fg98ffa748-d">An oil drop carrying three excess electrons held stationary between horizontal plates with a p.d. of 600 V.</desc><rect x="70" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="70" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="58" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">+</text><text x="58" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:700">−</text><circle cx="180" cy="110" r="7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180" y1="101" x2="180" y2="66.3" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="180,60 183.8,68.2 176.2,68.2" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="188" y="70" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">electric force</text><line x1="180" y1="119" x2="180" y2="153.7" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="180,160 176.2,151.8 183.8,151.8" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><text x="188" y="150" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8)">weight</text><text x="180" y="24" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">p.d. 600 V</text></svg>', 'An oil drop carrying three excess electrons held stationary between horizontal plates with a p.d. of 600 V.'),
('89c1c40c-42f6-5b9f-814b-145fc914a129', 'a6c1f6cd-641d-4d35-8950-b05e6c80ecf5', 'd1772ef2-4c08-4e93-86a4-2802dcbf78cc', 'a-level', '21.4', '9702 coursebook 21.4 · Force on a charge', 50, 50, 'Electrons accelerated from rest through 800 V enter, midway and parallel, between two horizontal plates 5.0 cm long and 2.0 cm apart with a p.d. of 100 V between them. A screen is 20 cm beyond the end of the plates. (a) Calculate the speed of the electrons. (b) Calculate the time spent between the plates and the vertical acceleration there. (c) Calculate the vertical deflection and vertical velocity on leaving the plates. (d) Calculate the total vertical deflection of the spot on the screen, in mm. Give only the answer to (d). Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C and mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '35.16 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) v = √(2 × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 800 ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹) = 1.68 × 10⁷ m s⁻¹. (b) t = 0.050 ÷ 1.676 × 10⁷ = 2.98 × 10⁻⁹ s. E = 100 ÷ 0.020 = 5000 V m⁻¹, so a = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ × 5000 ÷ 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ = 8.78 × 10¹⁴ m s⁻². (c) y₁ = ½at² = 0.5 × 8.782 × 10¹⁴ × (2.983 × 10⁻⁹)² = 0.00391 m. v_y = at = 8.782 × 10¹⁴ × 2.983 × 10⁻⁹ = 2.62 × 10⁶ m s⁻¹. (d) Beyond the plates it travels in a straight line for t₂ = 0.20 ÷ 1.676 × 10⁷ = 1.19 × 10⁻⁸ s, rising a further 2.619 × 10⁶ × 1.193 × 10⁻⁸ = 0.0313 m. Total deflection = 0.003906 + 0.03125 = 0.0352 m. In mm: 0.03516 × 1000 = 35.2. Mark scheme (7 marks). C1: ½mv² = eV. C1: t = L/v and a = eE/m. C1: y₁ = ½at². C1: v_y = at. M1: straight line beyond plates. C1: total deflection. A1: y = 35.2 mm.', 7, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 400 220" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgbacc65a1-t fgbacc65a1-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgbacc65a1-t">Deflecting an electron beam</title><desc id="fgbacc65a1-d">Electrons accelerated through 800 V enter midway between horizontal plates 5.0 cm long and 2.0 cm apart with 100 V between them; a screen is 20 cm beyond the plates.</desc><rect x="90" y="42" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="90" y="170" width="220" height="8" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="78" y="46" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">+</text><text x="78" y="174" font-size="14" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">−</text><line x1="110" y1="56" x2="110" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="110,164 107,157.7 113,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="140" y1="56" x2="140" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="140,164 137,157.7 143,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="170" y1="56" x2="170" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="170,164 167,157.7 173,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="200" y1="56" x2="200" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,164 197,157.7 203,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="230" y1="56" x2="230" y2="159.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="230,164 227,157.7 233,157.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke:none"/><line x1="26